out.push(A('**1** _Not until the fourth Saturday **did anybody ask** where the book was._ **2** _At no point **was the service log** requested._ **3** _What stopped the whole thing **was** a key._ **4** _It was the key **that** stopped it._ **5** _Only when the key was released **did anything move**._ **6** _**The eight we have no reason for are** the group the committee has to decide about._ _(or_ **the eight, for whom we have no reason, are…** _)_'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **In neither summary.** **The fault is that the paragraph put its qualification second, and a summary is made from first sentences.** **Both summarisers were accurate and both lost the same clause.**'));
out.push(A('_(No Practise line in x.7. The Language box in a Review & Mediate cycle collects the moves and carries no Practise item — the house pattern at every level of this series.)_'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the fourth mediation and the second that adds a reader, and the class should be shown how the two additions differ.** **4.7 added a question to the reader because the reader was going to act.** **5.7 adds a question to the summariser because the summariser has already acted** — **and the question is not a correction and must not sound like one: _which sentence did you take it from?_** **He will say the first, and that is a fact the writer cannot obtain from anybody else.** ⚠ **And the second half, which is the harder discipline: the committee member who wrote _about nine records a month_ is left entirely alone.** **Thirty-one minus twenty-two is nine, the subtraction is in the paragraph, and a reader given two numbers will subtract them.** **The writer invited it.** **A mediator who corrects him has spent the cycle on the one person who did nothing wrong.**'));
out.push(NOTE('**The unit\'s whole argument lands in this cycle and it is worth stating as two sentences on the board before Stage 3.** ⚠ **A reader keeps the end of a paragraph. A summariser takes its beginning.** **Those are two different people and every document is written for both.** **So the emphasis goes at the end for the reader, and the qualification goes inside the first claim for the quoter** — **which is Unit 4\'s rule about limits arriving at Unit 5 as a rule about position.** **Mrs Ajouz makes the connection herself in the dialogue and the class should be stopped there**: 4.5 said a limit in its own sentence will be separated by a quoter, and 5.7 says a limit in the second sentence will be dropped by a summariser. **Same fault, two mechanisms, and one repair.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Pair A, the dispensing figures)'));
