out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Of the three claims, the first and the second are the two that can be tested against a document anybody has, and the third is a claim about cost that this essay has no figures for.** **Both of the two are claims about what happens before a word is written.**',
  '**That a reader keeps almost nothing is the stronger of the two and the easier to demonstrate.** **A committee paper of nine hundred words reaches a committee as one line on an agenda, and that line is almost always the paper\'s first sentence.** ⚠ **The claim is usually stated as a complaint about attention, and it is not one: it is a fact about how documents travel.** **A reader who keeps four words has not failed; the four words are the document, and the only question is whether the writer chose them.**',
  '**That bad writing comes from an undecided purpose is harder to test and it is where the first claim leads.** **A writer who cannot say which sentence their paragraph exists for will emphasise every sentence, and a paragraph with three emphases has none.** ⚠ **The objection is that purpose is often decided by the time of writing and lost in the drafting**, which is true and does not rescue the claim: **a purpose that cannot survive a draft was a subject and not a purpose.**',
  '**Put together, the two claims make a third that neither makes alone.** **If a reader keeps the ends and a summariser takes the beginnings, a document has two audiences and must be built for both** — ⚠ **which is a question of cost, and that is where the third point was.**',
]));
out.push(A('**249 words, inside the band, two points named in paragraph one with a ground that could be wrong, an objection raised and answered in each body paragraph, and a conclusion that arrives at the omitted point and says so in the last clause.** ⚠ **The sentence that earns the band is _a purpose that cannot survive a draft was a subject and not a purpose._** **Fourteen words, it is in neither of the claims, and it is the sentence the essay exists to make.**'));
out.push(S('Stage ✓ · Unit 5 check'));
out.push(A('**A** **1** c _(did anybody ask)_   **2** b _(was the log)_   **3** a _(was)_   **4** c _(for whom)_   **5** b _(in dispute)_   **6** a _(placement)_   **7** c _(transferred)_   **8** b _(were)_'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Item 4 is the one that separates a class and it is not a grammar point most of them have been taught: _the eight for whom we have no reason_.** **_That_ and _which_ cannot follow a preposition**, so a relative clause with a fronted preposition takes _whom_ or _which_ and not _that_ — **and _which_ fails here because the antecedent is people.** **Teach the mechanical repair: if the preposition is at the front, the relative is _whom_ or _which_; if it is at the end, _that_ is available.** ⚠ **And item 1 is the inversion**, which about half of any class gets right by ear and cannot explain: **the auxiliary stands before the subject, and where there is no auxiliary you supply _do_.**'));
out.push(A('**B  Listening** **1** B   **2** C   **3** A   **4** A   **5** C   **6** B'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **Part 1 is three extracts with two questions each and the questions come in pairs that are easy to confuse: the first is almost always about what happened and the second about what somebody will do or thinks.** **Teach the pairing explicitly and have the class mark their papers before the recording: _happened_ against _will do_.** **Item 2 is where this is tested** — **the man says what the clerk in planning does and then says he will do it himself**, and candidates who have not separated the two questions take the planning clerk\'s practice as the answer to question 1. ⚠ **And item 5 is the distractor worth five minutes: option A, _it is inaccurate_, is contradicted in the first line of the extract** — _the agenda line is not wrong either_ — **and about a third of any class takes it anyway, because the extract is plainly about something being wrong.** **The word is in the recording attached to the opposite claim, which is the commonest wrong answer in every listening part at every level.**'));
